<http://data.silknow.org/object/8f5f4869-5f6e-3f47-a97b-86c357337d1d/observation/2>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The oldest Ottoman embroideries in the V&A date from the 16th or 17th centuries. They are either whole covers and wall hangings or fragments of them. They are decorated with large-scale, bold designs in red, blue, green and yellow, with some white and black.  In the 17th century the main designs were based on wavy parallel stems which run along the length of the fabric."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/8f5f4869-5f6e-3f47-a97b-86c357337d1d> .

