        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Panels from a hanging, linen embroidered with silk in regular surface darning and running stitch (border)\nThe border consists of a meander formed by an elongated red flower with a white centre linked by a narrow green leaf. To either side of this meander is a blue chintamani.\nThe field is decorated with undulating, vertical parallel stems which are blue with a central yellow line with round flowerheads. A green stem comes from the blue, bending in the opposite direction and curving round so that the large red and white blossom it bears crosses the blue stem. By curving in this way the green stem encloses a yellow chintamani.  This blossom contains a sprig with two pomegranates and a tulip in reserve.  A red and white blossom, identical to the ones in the border, grows from near the base of the green stem. There is a black chintamani (corroded) between the large red flowers."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/8f5f4869-5f6e-3f47-a97b-86c357337d1d> .

